module std::fs;

// File primitives (Rust's std::fs shape: functions returning values; errors
// are simulation/compile failures).
// Runtime-provided, like std::rand. std ships the PRIMITIVE only: format
// loaders (hex images, CSV stimulus, ...) are parsing libraries, not std.
//
//   read(path)             file bytes fill the declared array
//                          (`let rom: unsigned[8][256] = read("rom.bin");`
//                          little-endian packing for wider elements; a
//                          shorter file leaves the tail at 0, a longer one
//                          errors). A hardware/top initializer is a ROM image
//                          read by the compiler. A #[test] local is opened by
//                          the generated executable each time that test runs.
//   read_to_string(path)   UTF-8 file contents. The compiler bakes a
//                          hardware/top initializer; a #[test] owns runtime
//                          Char[] length and code-point storage.
//   exists(path)           runtime path probe in a #[test] (never fails)
